        "comments": "The signals of the built-in UART lines can be found on the expansion connector. The full pinout of the expansion connector can be found in the user guide of the device.\n\n| <code>\nSerial pinout:\n           |                   |                   |    |     SHIELD\n           |                   |        CPU        |    |_____________\n           |                   |___________________|                  \n 7: 3.3V   |                                                          \n41: GND    |                                                          \n45: TX     |       49         _____________________________         1 \n47: RX     |        o o o o o|o o o o o o o o o o o o o o o|o o o o o\n           |        o o o o o|o o o o o o o o o o o o o o o|o o o o o\n           |       50         -----------------------------         2\n           |__________________________________________________________\n</code> |\n\nThe UART lines are operating at TTL voltage levels, so if you want to connect it to your PC, you need a TTL-to-RS232 level shifter. See the [[http://nuwiki.openwrt.org/oldwiki/openwrtdocs/customizing/hardware/serial_console|Serial Console]] article for more informations.\n",
